.TH QUANT 1 "July 2026" "Quant 1.0.0" "Quant Language Tools"
.SH NAME
quant \- project manager for the Quant language
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quant
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B quant
is the project manager for Quant. It reads a \fBquant.toml\fR manifest in
the current directory and provides a unified interface for creating,
building, running, testing, linting, and documenting Quant projects
without having to invoke the individual tools directly.
.PP
Example manifest:
.PP
.RS
.nf
[project]
name    = "my-project"
version = "0.1.0"
entry   = "src/main.qa"
.fi
.RE
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init \fINAME\fR
Scaffold a new project in a directory named \fINAME\fR. Creates
\fBquant.toml\fR, \fBsrc/main.qa\fR (hello-world template), and
\fBtests/\fR.
.TP
.B build [\-\-release]
Compile the project. With \fB\-\-release\fR, enable optimisations.
Output is written to \fI.build/\fR.
.TP
.B run [\fIARGS\fR]
Compile and immediately execute the project, forwarding any extra
arguments to the program.
.TP
.B test [\fIFILE\fR]
Discover and run all test functions. Test files must match
\fI*_test.qa\fR inside the \fBtests/\fR directory (configurable in
\fBquant.toml\fR). Any function whose name begins with \fBtest_\fR and
takes no parameters is treated as a test case.
.br
Exits with status 1 if any test fails.
.TP
.B lint
Run
.BR wheatley (1)
over all source files in the project.
.TP
.B fmt [\-\-check]
Run
.BR quant\-fmt (1)
over all source files. With \fB\-\-check\fR, exit 1 if any file
would be changed (useful in CI).
.TP
.B doc [\-\-format \fIFMT\fR] [\-\-out \fIDIR\fR]
Generate API documentation from doc comments (\fI//\fR above public
functions). \fIFMT\fR is \fBhtml\fR (default) or \fBmd\fR. Output
goes to \fIdocs/api/\fR by default.
.TP
.B clean
Remove build artefacts (\fI.build/\fR).
.SH OPTIONS (all commands)
.TP
.B \-\-stdlib \fIDIR\fR
Override the standard library path, equivalent to
\fBQUANT_STDLIB\fR.
.SH QUANT.TOML FIELDS
.TP
.B [project] name
Project name (string, required).
.TP
.B [project] version
Semantic version string (required).
.TP
.B [project] entry
Relative path to the main source file (default: \fBsrc/main.qa\fR).
.TP
.B [project] stdlib
Override stdlib path for this project (optional).
.TP
.B [test] dir
Directory to search for test files (default: \fBtests/\fR).
.TP
.B [doc] out
Output directory for generated documentation (default: \fBdocs/api/\fR).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Command succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
Compilation error, test failure, lint error, or missing manifest.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QUANT_STDLIB
Standard library path, used when \fBstdlib\fR is not set in
\fBquant.toml\fR and \fB\-\-stdlib\fR is not passed.
.SH EXAMPLES
Create and run a new project:
.PP
.RS
.nf
quant init hello-world
cd hello-world
quant run
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run tests:
.PP
.RS
.B quant test
.RE
.PP
Check formatting and lint in CI:
.PP
.RS
.nf
quant fmt \-\-check
quant lint
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glados (1),
.BR glados\-repl (1),
.BR quant\-fmt (1),
.BR wheatley (1),
.BR glados\-lsp (1)
